WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.010
"New year, new me."

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.481
It's a phrase pretty much everyone says as
they approach the end of one year and the

00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:06.580
beginning of another.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.620
Turns out, it's a phrase the folks at Netflix
must have been uttering as they put together

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.880
their line-up for January 2020.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:19.019
Beginning January 2020, Netflix subscribers
can sink their teeth into four stellar action

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.840
flicks - and let it suffice to say: It's all
killer, no filler.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:23.960
Thrill ride, anyone?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.760
Based on the Marvel Comics character, Ghost
Rider stars Nicolas Cage as the titular superhero

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.480
- and rest assured, he's not your average
motorcycle stuntman turned fiery avenger on

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:33.980
wheels.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.220
That's coming your way on January 1st.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.420
"Time to clear the air."

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.220
"Heh heh haha."

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.219
Meanwhile, both installments of Quentin Tarantino's
epic Kill Bill films will be ready for your

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.140
viewing pleasure on January 1st.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:56.600
In a career-defining performance, Uma Thurman
plays Beatrix Kiddo, an ex-assassin obsessively

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.460
hunting down her former lover - the mysterious
Bill.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.520
Meanwhile, she exacts her revenge on all the
men and women who have betrayed her over the

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.020
years.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.040
And beginning on January 31st, you can check
out the 2017 action-thriller American Assassin,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.820
starring Dylan O'Brien as a man hellbent on
avenging the death of his fiancée after she's

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.960
murdered by terrorists.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.940
Are you a big fan of fantasy films?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.420
You're officially in luck: Netflix will be
bringing plenty of magic into our lives - and

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:23.920
soon.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:29.440
On January 1st, Guillermo del Toro's sprawling,
Oscar-winning dark fantasy Pan's Labyrinth

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.800
hits the streaming service.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.000
The story involves a young girl who discovers
a mythical world of which she is the ruler.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.140
"No No!"

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.240
Oh, and you'll definitely want to check out
the second and third movies in Peter Jackson's

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.570
Lord of the Rings trilogy: The Two Towers
and The Return of the King will both be available

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.060
for streaming beginning on January 1st.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.320
Here's a New Year's resolution for you: Don't
let a drama-free day go by in January 2020.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.580
There are loads of acclaimed dramas coming
to Netflix - including Catch Me If You Can

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.120
starring Leonardo DiCaprio.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.360
He plays a brilliant con artist and bank robber
on the run from an FBI agent, played by Tom

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:08.860
Hanks.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.560
The film is a total delight, particularly
if you're into all sorts of wily cat-and-mouse

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.320
shenanigans.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.060
"My name is Frank Taylor, I'm a co-pilot for
PAN-AM.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:23.300
I'd like to cash this check here and then
I'd like to take you out for a steak dinner."

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.800
Let the games begin on January 1st.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.120
Another Leonardo DiCaprio film is coming to
Netflix that same day - and it's quite the

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:30.980
mind-melter.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.540
Inception involves a burglar who can creep
into people's dreams and pluck out all their

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.040
secrets.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.760
Prepare to have your brain scrambled by this
beguiling, endlessly entertaining film.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.480
There's even more gripping goodness coming
your way on January 1st, including the whip-smart

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.690
comedy-drama Up in the Air, starring George
Clooney and Anna Kendrick.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.460
On January 18th, The Bling Ring starts streaming.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.440
Based on a true story, this stylish drama
involves a group of crafty teenagers who figure

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.860
out how to rob the luxurious homes of celebrities.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.080
In the mood for something completely different?

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.850
We Are Your Friends starts streaming on January
27th, and it's a music drama that just so

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:10.140
happens to be directed by Max Joseph of Catfish
fame.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:15.459
Get ready to laugh, because Netflix is bringing
plenty of classic comedies to the streamer

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.880
in January 2020.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.960
First up is Ferris Bueller's Day Off, an iconic
comedy about cutting school in favor of all

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.620
sorts of mischievous highjinx.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.140
That will be available to stream on January
1st.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.520
That's also the day you can check out the
classic 1971 musical comedy Willy Wonka &amp; the

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.520
Chocolate Factory.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.400
"Boy what a great series this would have been!"

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:35.700
"Wonka!"

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.680
"This is kinda strange."

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.540
"Yes, strange Charlie, but it's fun - haha!"

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.400
And if that's not quite enough whimsy for
you, Tim Burton's 2005 update, Charlie and

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.740
the Chocolate Factory, also begins streaming
on January 1st.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:49.660
That's not all.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.900
Hitch starring Will Smith is coming to Netflix
on January 1st, along with the zany romp Yes

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.300
Man, starring Jim Carrey.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:02.560
Then, on January 15th, Netflix starts streaming
the cutesy 2002 teen comedy Big Fat Liar.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.840
Sure, why not?

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.900
There's only one stand-up comedy special coming
to Netflix in January 2020, but it's one that

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.460
you absolutely should not miss.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:15.660
Comedian Fortune Feimster brings her first-ever
Netflix comedy special to the streamer on

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.000
January 21st.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.099
In Fortune Feimster: Sweet &amp; Salty, the Office
Christmas Party star reminisces about her

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:24.710
childhood, including her experiences as a
Girl Scout.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:29.669
She also opens up about her family's absurd
relationship with a certain chicken wing restaurant

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:33.720
chain, and reveals how one film helped her
come to terms with her sexuality.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.080
Scared?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.200
Perhaps you should be.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.880
Netflix is adding tons of amazing horror films
and thrillers to the streaming service in

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.220
January 2020.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:47.419
On January 1st, you can watch The Ring, a
supernatural thriller about a cursed videotape

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.120
that kills anyone who watches it within seven
days.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.639
That same day, you can check out The Talented
Mr. Ripley, a twisted thriller starring Matt

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.580
Damon as a charming con artist and serial
killer.

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:02.819
Finally, What Lies Beneath is a supernatural
tale starring Harrison Ford and Michelle Pfeiffer

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.280
as a well-to-do couple living in a haunted
house.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.640
Expect plenty of twists and turns in that
one.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:19.180
Then, on January 30th, Briam De Palma's Raising
Cain hits Netflix.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.360
This underrated gem stars John Lithgow as
Dr. Carter Nix, a brilliant child psychologist

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.750
suffering from multiple personality disorder.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:31.150
Following a shocking discovery, one of those
personalities - the titular Cain - comes to

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.100
the fore and Carter's actions grow increasingly
violent.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:38.480
This is some trashy, twisted fun that's chockablock
with unforgettables performances - all of

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.920
which come from Lithgow.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:45.300
A handful of Netflix originals are presenting
their final seasons, including Anne with an

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.860
E on January 3rd and The Ranch on January
24th.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.630
Other shows will be continuing their highly
successful runs.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:55.969
Keep an eye out for the sixth season of the
comedy series Grace and Frankie on January

00:05:55.969 --> 00:05:56.460
15th.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.360
Then there's the second season of the runaway
hit Sex Education on January 17th.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.780
Meanwhile, the spellbinding third season of
Chilling Adventures of Sabrina is coming for

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:10.909
you on January 24th, and the second season
of the documentary series I AM A KILLER starts

00:06:10.909 --> 00:06:12.760
streaming on January 31st.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:17.480
Of course, we'd be remiss not to mention what's
arguably the best TV offering on Netflix:

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.080
The sixth and final season of BoJack Horseman
arrives on the last day of January, and you

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.680
definitely won't want to miss that.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:24.920
"Today sucks.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.380
The story of my life is that I never get anything
nice."

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.460
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:33.960
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.180
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

